WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.919
Welcome to The Logic Grid: eleven puzzle
games, free to play in your browser.

2
00:00:06.269 --> 00:00:09.299
Here is a quick tour of everything on the
site.

3
00:00:10.349 --> 00:00:13.733
This is the front page, at thelogicgrid.com.

4
00:00:13.753 --> 00:00:19.395
Every puzzle here can be solved by reasoning
alone. No guessing needed.

5
00:00:20.445 --> 00:00:25.225
At the top: your Account, and Look, which
changes the colors of the page.

6
00:00:26.275 --> 00:00:32.249
Each card is a game. Choose Play to start, or
Rules and how to play to learn it first.

7
00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:38.156
The Fantastical Logic Grid: story logic
puzzles. Read the clues,

8
00:00:38.176 --> 00:00:43.966
mark the grid, and work out who did what.
Every case is a brand new story.

9
00:00:45.016 --> 00:00:52.206
NINETIMESNINE: number puzzles from 4 by 4 up
to 9 by 9, with five ways to play.

10
00:00:53.256 --> 00:00:57.297
Cage Math: fill each cage so its numbers make
the target,

11
00:00:57.317 --> 00:01:00.745
with every number once in each row and column.

12
00:01:01.795 --> 00:01:06.830
Sum Cross: a crossword of numbers, where every
run adds up to its clue.

13
00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.905
Picture Grid: shade the cells each row and
column calls for,

14
00:01:11.925 --> 00:01:15.177
and a hidden picture appears for your gallery.

15
00:01:16.227 --> 00:01:19.959
More or Less: every number once in each row
and column,

16
00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:23.267
and the signs between cells say which is less.

17
00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:26.492
Skyline: build a city of towers.

18
00:01:26.512 --> 00:01:32.425
The numbers at the edge say how many you can
see, because tall ones hide short ones.

19
00:01:33.475 --> 00:01:36.118
Star Field: place stars so every row,

20
00:01:36.138 --> 00:01:40.750
column and region has the same number, and no
two stars touch.

21
00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:45.184
Loop Line: draw one closed loop around the
dots,

22
00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:49.395
so each number shows how many of its sides the
loop uses.

23
00:01:50.445 --> 00:01:54.322
Island Bridges: join every island with
straight bridges,

24
00:01:54.342 --> 00:01:57.763
so each has its number and all of them
connect.

25
00:01:58.813 --> 00:02:03.955
Crossword: fill the grid with words that match
the clues, Across and Down.

26
00:02:05.005 --> 00:02:07.453
Every game has its own rules page,

27
00:02:07.473 --> 00:02:12.195
with a narrated how-to video, so you can learn
before you play.

28
00:02:13.245 --> 00:02:18.392
Inside The Fantastical Logic Grid, How to play
teaches you step by step,

29
00:02:18.412 --> 00:02:22.867
and the Introduction video shows everything
the game can do.

30
00:02:23.917 --> 00:02:28.441
See the games has this tour, and a one-minute
video for each game.

31
00:02:29.491 --> 00:02:32.313
Guests can start a few new puzzles a day.

32
00:02:32.333 --> 00:02:36.574
One free account gives you unlimited puzzles
in every game.

33
00:02:36.924 --> 00:02:42.429
Sign in once, and your saves, stats and
settings follow you to every device.

34
00:02:43.479 --> 00:02:48.877
Messages and news has notes from the team, and
replies to anything you sent.

35
00:02:49.927 --> 00:02:54.557
Submit Puzzle Ideas lets you make your own
puzzle, step by step.

36
00:02:54.907 --> 00:02:58.165
It checks your puzzle has exactly one answer,

37
00:02:58.185 --> 00:03:02.779
gives you a PDF to print, and saves it to your
Saved puzzles.

38
00:03:03.829 --> 00:03:09.006
Choose which puzzle to make, and the wizard
asks only what that puzzle needs.

39
00:03:09.026 --> 00:03:11.403
It has its own how-to video, too.

40
00:03:12.453 --> 00:03:18.214
Something not right? Report a Problem tells
the team, with a screenshot if you like.

41
00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:20.420
Where your device allows it,

42
00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:26.351
Install the app puts every game on your home
screen or desktop, and they work offline.

43
00:03:27.401 --> 00:03:30.879
Follow The Logic Grid for the daily puzzle and
news.

44
00:03:31.929 --> 00:03:34.559
There is a new daily puzzle every day,

45
00:03:34.579 --> 00:03:38.842
the same one for everyone, so you can compare
with friends.

46
00:03:39.892 --> 00:03:44.181
Printables has free puzzles to print, each
with its answer key.

47
00:03:45.231 --> 00:03:50.863
And for teachers, Educators has free printable
puzzle packages for the classroom.

48
00:03:51.913 --> 00:03:55.370
Pick your puzzle, or make your own. Happy
puzzling!

